      "assertions": [
        "Actual signed native dtmf.send freezes original source, logical ID, method, duration and physical recipients. HTTP cannot borrow native custody.",
        "Native and initial/established SIP output use actual original frames/calls and negotiated RFC4733 profile. The exact30-second sequence retains terminal packets. Long fanout schedules overlap and settle partial refusal honestly.",
        "Named source-send/recipient-receive grants are independent of RTP/subscription. Current withdrawal, cancellation, partial writes, unknown outcomes, writer fact outage and restart never redeliver original work.",
        "Private native, retained SIP, SIP-primary and fresh SIP-candidate roles exclude held/public physical siblings, survive captured lifetime changes and preserve current permission checks. An unfinished private INFO prefix cannot lend its tail to original return or public recovery."
      ]
    },
    "u6-req-0113": {
